menu "BlueAudio Puck: equaliser"

    config PUCK_EQ_BANDS
        int "Number of parametric bands per channel"
        default 5
        range 1 10
        help
            Each band is one biquad section per channel. Bands sitting at 0 dB
            are bypassed at runtime and cost nothing, so this sets the ceiling
            rather than a fixed price. Five is the usual tone-control layout:
            low shelf, three bells, high shelf.

    config PUCK_EQ_ENABLED_AT_BOOT
        bool "Enable the equaliser at start-up"
        default n
        help
            Off by default so the puck starts out transparent. The bands begin
            flat in any case, so turning this on changes nothing until a band
            is given some gain.

endmenu
